From: OpenHarmony PC Developer Community
Subject: [PATCH] boxes 2.3.1: add OHOS platform branch to config.h

The OHOS (HarmonyOS) bionic libc requires _GNU_SOURCE to expose common
POSIX functions such as strdup(), strcasecmp() and strncasecmp() in
declarations. Without these, clang emits implicit-function-declaration
errors.

The existing config.h conditionals cover Linux (glibc), macOS, Solaris,
FreeBSD and MinGW, but OHOS falls through to the else-branch that
defines only _POSIX_SOURCE (POSIX.1-1990), which does not expose them.
Fold OHOS into the existing Linux/glibc/GNU branch: bionic recognises
_GNU_SOURCE and exposes the same set of functions under it.
---
 src/config.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/config.h b/src/config.h
index 4a6d5f8..a9c0e12 100644
--- a/src/config.h
+++ b/src/config.h
@@ -21,7 +21,7 @@
 #define CONFIG_H


-#if defined(__linux__) || defined(__GLIBC__) || defined(__GNU__)
+#if defined(__OHOS__) || defined(__OHOS) || defined(__linux__) || defined(__GLIBC__) || defined(__GNU__)

 #define _GNU_SOURCE

--
2.45.1

